From b9acec2a6dbe7ea030613e74d3483636919725a8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ericek111 <erik.brocko@letemsvetemapplem.eu>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 01:24:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 46/50] linux_page: refuse opportunistic higher-order page
 allocations

TTM fills a BO by asking for order 10, then 9, ... with __GFP_NORETRY
before it takes single pages. Linux makes those attempts cheap. In the
port, each one became a physically contiguous IOBufferMemoryDescriptor,
which makes xnu walk physical memory under the page-queue lock. On a
fresh boot the walk succeeds. After ~40 minutes of desktop use memory is
fragmented and each 2-4 MB walk fails after ~350 ms. Creating an 8 MB BO
then took 740 ms (vm/guest/tools/gemlat), and WindowServer creates one
for most new Metal textures: under 1 fps, ordered flips timing out
(frames shown unpublished), and stutter for everything else waiting on
the page-queue lock.

linux_alloc_pages now returns NULL for order > 0 with __GFP_NORETRY, so
TTM takes single pages from the chunk pool right away. 8 MB create:
740 ms -> 0.8 ms, and 0.9 ms with 6 GB of memory deliberately fragmented.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 override/src/linux_page.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/gpu-port/xkpi/override/src/linux_page.c b/gpu-port/xkpi/override/src/linux_page.c
index ee6df73..cf39226 100644
--- a/gpu-port/xkpi/override/src/linux_page.c
+++ b/gpu-port/xkpi/override/src/linux_page.c
@@ -100,6 +100,15 @@ linux_alloc_pages(gfp_t flags, unsigned int order)
 	unsigned long npages = 1UL << order;
 	int req = VM_ALLOC_WIRED;
 
+	/*
+	 * __GFP_NORETRY marks an opportunistic higher order: TTM asks for 4 MB, then 2 MB, ... before taking single
+	 * pages. xnu has no cheap contiguous attempt. Every contiguous allocation walks physical memory under the
+	 * page-queue lock, and once memory is fragmented a 2-4 MB walk fails after ~350 ms (vm/guest/tools/gemlat: an
+	 * 8 MB BO took 740 ms, and WindowServer's frames waited on it). Refuse those orders, so the caller falls back
+	 * to single pages from the chunk pool.
+	 */
+	if (order > 0 && (flags & __GFP_NORETRY) != 0)
+		return (NULL);
 	if ((flags & M_ZERO) != 0)
 		req |= VM_ALLOC_ZERO;
 	if (order == 0 && (flags & GFP_DMA32) == 0)
